   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): REQUEST CHANGES** — head fd228d5e41bca0882da3341a7b55873596285f7e\n\n1. **Low — `App/README.md:21-25`.** The README still calls its command the one CI runs (\"unsigned, as CI does\"), but the command has no `-parallel-testing-enabled NO`. So a Mac session that tries to reproduce a CI failure from the README still runs the clones, and sees the 270-360 s tests and the web-view timeouts that CI no longer has. Fix: add `-parallel-testing-enabled NO` to that command, or say why it differs from CI.\n2. **Low — `.github/workflows/ci.yml:199-200` and the PR body.** The comment and the PR body describe the symptom but not where it comes from. The clones started with `parallelizable = \"YES\"` in `App/SwiftHFR.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/SwiftHFR.xcscheme:35`, which #717 (LOT-163) added and which nothing has changed since. The CI flag overrides it, so the fix works and stays narrow. But Xcode runs from the scheme, and any other `xcodebuild test` call, still use clones. Fix: name #717 and the scheme setting in the comment, so the next reader knows which setting the flag cancels.\n3. **Detail — no proof the fix works yet.** The PR is a draft, so the App job failed at the draft gate in 3 s. Nothing has run on macOS at this head. The PR body already says the timing will come from the first ready run. Before merging, check that run: the App job is green, the 4 tests named in #801 pass, and the test phase is well under the step's 45 minutes.\n\nVerified by the reviewer: flag is valid and overrides the scheme's `parallelizable`; no clones with it off; 16 min fits the 45 min step and 75 min job limits; no test touched. No build or tests run (Linux session).\n\n(Verdict relayed verbatim from the review sub-agent, round 1 of 2.)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
